   "line": [
    "Bf4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Our development is excellent — a bishop to f4, a rook to d1, and a simple plan of queenside expansion with a3 and b4.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 3080,
   "fen": "r2q1rk1/pp1bbppp/2n1pn2/8/2P2B2/2NQ1N2/PP2BPPP/R4RK1 b - - 6 12",
   "line": [
    "O-O",
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "I'm biased toward this position because it occurs in the Alapin too: after a bishop check on b5, a knight to d7, d4, a6, a bishop to e2, a knight to c5, a knight to f3, c6, you get an identical structure with the same queenside-expansion plan — White a smidge better and hard for Black to play.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 3135.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkb1r/pppbpppp/8/3n4/3P4/8/PPP1BPPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "The same pawn structure, the same plan — Black has to play very carefully to equalize. Our opponent's knight to c6...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 3136.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/2n5/3n4/3P4/8/PPP1BPPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Nc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...is awkward; it walks into c4.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 3139.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/2n5/3n4/2PP4/8/PP2BPPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "c4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 3141.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/2n2n2/8/2PP4/8/PP2BPPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 1 7",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 3143,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/2n2n2/3P4/2P5/8/PP2BPPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": "According to the computer I should have played a knight to f3 here, not pushed d5 prematurely — just develop.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 3164.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/5n2/3Pn3/2P5/5N2/PP2BPPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 2 8",
   "line": [
    "Ne5",
    "Nf3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black's knight is horribly placed; Black has to contest with c5, and White is much better. Instead I played d5, and Black can actually equalize.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 3175,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/5n2/3P4/2P5/5n2/PP2BPPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "Nxf3+"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black is supposed to take on f3.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 3176.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/5n2/3P4/2P5/5B2/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "Bxf3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 3180,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppb1ppp/4pn2/3P4/2P5/5B2/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": "If Black plays e6, the correct move is e5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 3187.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/5n2/3Pn3/2P5/5N2/PP2BPPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 2 8",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "That was the whole point of the knight to f3 — to stop Black pushing the e-pawn — but I didn't calculate far enough.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 3195,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppb1ppp/4Pn2/8/2P5/5B2/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "e6",
    "dxe6",
    "Nxf3+",
    "Bxf3"
   ],
   "spoken": "I trusted my intuition: take en passant and grab b7.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 3198.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/ppp2ppp/4bn2/8/2P5/5B2/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "Bxe6"
   ],
   "spoken": "But the b7 pawn can't easily be captured.",
