  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 3212.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/ppp2ppp/4bn2/8/2P5/5B2/PP3PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 11",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "...and recaptures on c4 with an advantage. If you check on a4, Black covers with a pawn.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 3219.5,
   "fen": "r2Qkb1r/ppp2ppp/4bn2/8/2P5/5B2/PP3PPP/RNB1K2R b KQkq - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "Qxd8+"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black will cover it with a pawn; and if we lead with the queen trade, Black just recaptures with the rook.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 3225.5,
   "fen": "3rkb1r/pBp2ppp/4bn2/8/2P5/8/PP3PPP/RNB1K2R b KQk - 0 12",
   "line": [
    "Rxd8",
    "Bxb7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Same thing — you can take on b7, but Black plays a bishop capture on c4...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 3232,
   "fen": "3rk2r/pBp2ppp/4bn2/2b5/2P5/8/PP3PPP/RNB1K2R w KQk - 1 13",
   "line": [
    "Bc5"
   ],
   "spoken": "...or a bishop to c5, and it's anybody's game — not an obvious idea at all.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 3235.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppb1ppp/4Pn2/4n3/2P5/5N2/PP2BPPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "It emphasizes not trusting your opponent's ideas.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 3243,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/5n2/3Pn3/2P5/5N2/PP2BPPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 2 8",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "If your opponent plays a move and it's obvious why, still ask: can I achieve what I wanted?",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 3252,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/5nn1/3P4/2P5/5N2/PP2BPPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 3 9",
   "line": [
    "Ng6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Which here was freeing the kingside. Our opponent just trusted us with a knight to g6...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 3255,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/5nn1/3P4/2P4P/5N2/PP2BPP1/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "h4"
   ],
   "spoken": "...and walked into h4, a really nasty move.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 3260.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbppp1/5nn1/3P3p/2P4P/5N2/PP2BPP1/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "h5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black is in trouble; he had to play h5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 3270,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbppp1/5nn1/3P3p/2P4P/3B1N2/PP3PP1/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 1 10",
   "line": [
    "Bd3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now the g6 knight is loosely protected, so you slide the bishop to d3.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 3274.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbpppp/5nn1/3P4/2P4P/5N2/PP2BPP1/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "Remember this: start with h4, provoke h5, then slide the bishop up...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 3277,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppbppp1/5nn1/3P3p/2P4P/3B1N2/PP3PP1/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 1 10",
   "line": [
    "h5",
    "Bd3"
   ],
   "spoken": "...threatening to ruin Black's kingside with a bishop capture on g6.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 3286,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pppb1pp1/4pnn1/3P3p/2P4P/3B1N2/PP3PP1/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": "You don't have to do it immediately — the engine says castle first.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
